<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancho II of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1036–<a href="/years/1072">1072</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sancho the Strong · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimenez-dynasty">Jiménez dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancho II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1065 to 1072, the eldest son of Ferdinand I, who divided his realms among his children. Aided by his commander Rodrigo Díaz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a>, he fought his brothers and took León and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. He was killed in 1072 while besieging his sister Urraca at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamora">Zamora</a>, and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> then reunited Castile and León.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sancho-ii-of-castile.jpg" alt="Sancho II of Castile" width="320" height="593" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sancho_II_de_Le%C3%A3o_e_Castela_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>At his death in 1065 he divided his realms among his sons: Castile went to the eldest, <b>Sancho II</b>, León to Alfonso VI and Galicia to García.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>From 1065 Castile was a kingdom in its own right under <b>Sancho II</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-castile">County of Castile</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Zamora, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in Zamora, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.5,-5.76&amp;year=1059" aria-label="Zamora on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4410 684 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Sancho II of Castile"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4860 954h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4860 954h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.5,-5.76&amp;year=1059">What was here in 1059? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
